course: dictionary
lesson: 15039
title: Retaliate: hitting back
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: To retaliate means to do something bad back to someone who has hurt or attacked you. It is another way of saying hit back. «When Sam pushed Max, Max did not retaliate. He walked away and told the teacher.»
explain: Look at the clues around the word. Someone has to hurt or attack you first, and then you do something bad in return. «The lions were angry, but the zebras did not retaliate; they just ran.» If nobody has hurt you, there is nothing to retaliate against.
explain: Retaliate is often followed by against or by. «The country chose to retaliate against the attack.» «The angry boy began to retaliate by throwing sand.» To check your meaning, swap in hit back. If the sentence still makes sense, you have it.
explain: Schools ask pupils not to retaliate, because hitting back usually makes a bad situation worse. Tell a trusted adult instead. «If someone hurts you, do not retaliate. Tell a grown-up.»
fact: Retaliate means to do something bad back to someone who has hurt or attacked you.
fact: Retaliate is another way of saying hit back.
fact: Retaliate is a verb, so it changes: retaliates, retaliated, retaliating.
fact: Phrases to know: retaliate against someone, or retaliate by doing something.
fact: In school rules, pupils are told not to retaliate but to tell an adult.
exercise: «When the boy pushed her, Ruby decided not to retaliate.» What did Ruby decide not to do? | Cry | Say thank you | Tell an adult | *Push him back
exercise: Which word means to hit back? | Apologise | Wander | *Retaliate | Forgive
exercise: «After Jo tripped him, Ravi did not retaliate. He told the teacher instead.» What does retaliate mean here? | To run away and hide | *To hit back after being hurt | To say sorry for tripping someone | To smile and wave
test: «The town was attacked, and the country chose to retaliate against the attackers.» What does retaliate against mean here? | Build a new bridge | Say sorry to the attackers | Leave the town quietly | *Hit back at the people who attacked
test: «The angry boy began to retaliate ___ throwing sand.» Which word fills the gap? | *by | about | because | with
exam: Why do schools tell pupils not to retaliate when someone hurts them? | Because retaliate means to forget | Because it is always fun to hit back | Because it helps you win the fight | *Hitting back usually makes things worse, so tell a trusted adult
